Gate secondary-CPU start on eMMC init (BCB cleared + SWEETLOG running).

0144 gave us the safe secondary-CPU marks, but the CPU1-timeout panic still
happens BEFORE onc_emmc_init() clears the Android BCB / starts the SWEETLOG
flusher, so the reset lands back in the recovery partition (iOS image): a
recovery loop with no adb and no log.  (0144's IMEM restart_reason does not
override ABL's BCB boot-recovery decision.)

0145 (2 files):

  iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
    - new C-linkage `volatile int sweet_emmc_ready` (defined for ONC builds);
    - startAll(): the boot CPU is started and verified exactly as today, then
      the remaining CPUs are gated on `sweet_emmc_ready`, polling every 1 ms
      (onc_spin_us) for up to `sweetemmcgate=<secs>` (default 30 s, 0 = no
      gate).  Logs the gate start/release/timeout and then continues with the
      unchanged per-CPU start/SGI1 handshake.

  bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
    - onc_emmc_init() sets `sweet_emmc_ready = 1` AFTER the 0133 BCB clear and
      AFTER the 0132 SWEETLOG flusher has been started, printing
      `SWEET CPU: eMMC ready, SMP may start`;
    - panic-time flush: `sweet_emmc_log_flush_panic()` (called from the 0137
      PE_halt_restart hook before the reset fallback) wakes the 0132 flusher
      thread repeatedly for <=1 s so the console ring - which already contains
      the panic text (and the 0144 mark/stage line) - is written to the eMMC
      log tail before the watchdog bite.  Other CPUs are still running there:
      the panic path calls halt_all_cpus() only AFTER PEHaltRestart returns.

